          "path": "_m/d/j/n/e/canaveral-national-seashore-wp/colletes-titusensis-m-back-bre.jpg",
          "filename": "Colletes titusensis, M, Back, Brevard co., Honda, U.S 2013-11-19-07.51.39 ZS PMax (10955045284).jpg",
          "caption": "Rarity here.  This is species was described in the 1950s, named after the town it was collected near and only a handful of specimens have ever been collected that I am aware of.  In fact it is so rare that it was on our list of \"missing\" species, published in 2011.  So it is nice to see this species and, indeed, it was collected at Cape Canaveral National Seashore, whose nearest town is.....Titusville.  Picture taken by Wayne Boo\n\nCanon Mark II 5D, Zerene Stacker, 65mm Canon MP-E 1-5X macro lens,  Twin Macro Flash,  F5.0,  ISO 100,  Shutter Speed 200",
          "alt": "Rarity here.  This is species was described in the 1950s, named after the town it was collected near and only a handful of specimens have ever been collected that I am aware of.  In fact it is so rare that it was on our list of \"missing\" species, published in 2011.  So it is nice to see this species and, indeed, it was collected at Cape Canaveral National Seashore, whose nearest town is.....Titusville.  Picture taken by Wayne Boo\n\nCanon Mark II 5D, Zerene Stacker, 65mm Canon MP-E 1-5X macro lens,  Twin Macro Flash,  F5.0,  ISO 100,  Shutter Speed 200",
          "width": 2303,
          "height": 3684,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "USGS Bee Inventory and Monitoring Lab from Beltsville, USA",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colletes_titusensis,_M,_Back,_Brevard_co.,_Honda,_U.S_2013-11-19-07.51.39_ZS_PMax_(10955045284).jpg",
